============================================================================
THE ZERO-PARAMETER NODE AGAINST THE MEASURED SEATS
============================================================================
  a (the only fitted quantity) = 17.715561710 MeV^1/2

  seat     sqrt(m) measured        predicted       residual     relative
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------
  tau          42.152817225     42.153083765     -2.665e-04       -6.32 ppm
  e             0.714841906      0.714821289     +2.062e-05      +28.84 ppm
  mu           10.279026000     10.278780076     +2.459e-04      +23.93 ppm

  residuals sum to +2.44e-15 -- identically zero, since a is their mean,
  so only two of the three are independent and no seat can be off on its own.

============================================================================
WHERE THE BREAKING SITS, ON EACH READING
============================================================================
  ADDITIVE on sqrt(m) -- largest first:   tau (-2.67e-04), mu (+2.46e-04), e (+2.06e-05)
  MULTIPLICATIVE      -- largest first:   e (+28.8 ppm), mu (+23.9 ppm), tau (-6.3 ppm)

  The two orderings disagree: absolutely the tau carries most, relatively the electron
  does, by 1.2x over the muon and 5x over the tau. That is not evidence
  either way -- it is arithmetic. The electron's seat ratio is the smallest of the three
  (0.0403 against 2.3794), so any absolute perturbation looks largest there
  in relative terms whatever its origin.

============================================================================
SO THE TEST DOES NOT BITE, AND THIS IS WHAT WOULD MAKE IT
============================================================================
  The prediction 'the breaking is electron-localised' is only testable once the spurion's
  form is fixed, because the two natural forms rank the seats oppositely. What the emergent
  reading owes is therefore not a size but a FORM: does the doping perturb sqrt(m)
  additively (a shift of the seat) or multiplicatively (a rescaling of the hopping)?

  Those are distinguishable. An additive spurion breaks the circulant structure itself and
  would show up as a departure from the Parseval identity Q = 1/3 + A^2/6; a multiplicative
  one preserves the circulant and moves only A and phi. The Parseval identity is exact on
  the measured masses by construction, so it cannot discriminate either -- but a FOURTH
  measured mass would, and the sector has none.

  Recording the negative result: the emergent-Z3 reading makes no further prediction that
  the three charged-lepton masses can test. It stands or falls on the spurion, and three
  numbers with one fitted scale leave two residuals, which is exactly the freedom two
  unknowns (A and phi) already use up.
